{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Target platform is the Spring XD 1.1 codeline (built on Spring Framework); Java 8 is adopted as the baseline JDK since U5 explicitly requires Java lambdas, while retaining compatibility for building/running on the supported server and embedded-jar deployment models.",
    "Keep the existing Gradle-based build; Windows build support (U3) is achieved by fixing path-separator handling, line-ending issues, and shell-specific build/test steps rather than introducing a separate Windows build system.",
    "Spark Streaming processors (U5) are implemented as standard XD stream processor modules in two variants: one in Java using Java 8 lambdas and one in Scala, both against the Spark Streaming API, with sample topologies demonstrating the capability.",
    "Pig support (U2) is delivered as a sample XD batch job module bundling a reference Pig script, sample data, configuration, and documentation.",
    "Kafka upgrade (U7) is done by backporting XD-specific Kafka changes into Spring Integration Kafka first, then replacing the custom code in XD with the SI Kafka GA release and adapting XD modules to the GA API.",
    "Hadoop upgrade (U8) moves XD from the pre-GA Spring Hadoop (SHDP) dependency to the SHDP GA release, adapting to any API/behavior changes and re-testing Hadoop-dependent modules.",
    "Windows acceptance testing (U4) uses a dedicated Windows AMI on EC2 pre-provisioned with JDK, Gradle, and XD; the acceptance suite is executed from a Jenkins CI job targeting that node, with environment-flaky tests quarantined and tracked.",
    "Documentation remains in the existing AsciiDoc/DocBook toolchain; the PDF reference guide (U6) is regenerated from updated sources so the copyright year change propagates everywhere.",
    "Migration support (U1) is delivered as a documented migration guide plus a validated, ported sample custom module rather than automated migration tooling."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "A single developer performs all work; estimates are effort in 8-hour workdays, not elapsed calendar time, and exclude leave, meetings unrelated to this increment, and organizational overhead.",
    "XD 1.0 and 1.1 source code, historical release notes, and issue trackers are available to derive the 1.0-to-1.1 migration deltas.",
    "SI Kafka GA and SHDP GA artifacts are publicly released and do not contain undocumented breaking changes beyond normal GA API stabilization.",
    "Existing CI infrastructure (Jenkins) and an AWS/EC2 account with permissions to create and manage Windows AMIs are available at no additional development effort.",
    "Hadoop, Pig, Kafka, and Spark test environments can be run locally or in pseudo-distributed/embedded mode; no production-grade cluster provisioning is in scope.",
    "Windows support scope is limited to building XD and running the acceptance test suite on Windows; it is not a full production certification on Windows.",
    "U5 scope is demonstration-grade Spark Streaming processors with tests and documentation, not production hardening or performance tuning.",
    "Each activity estimate includes its own unit testing and focused documentation; cross-cutting integration/regression testing and release documentation are estimated as separate activities."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Increment analysis and development environment setup",
      "activity_description": "Set up the development environment (JDK 8, Gradle, IDE, forks/branches), review the XD 1.1 codebase, and analyze the deltas relevant to all eight user stories to plan the increment.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "U1 - 1.0 to 1.1 migration guide and custom module porting",
      "activity_description": "Analyze API and module-model changes between XD 1.0 and 1.1, write the migration guide for operationalizing existing pipelines, and port a representative custom module to 1.1 to validate the documented steps.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "U2 - Pig job sample module",
      "activity_description": "Create a reference Pig script with sample data, package it as an XD batch job module with configuration, test it end-to-end in XD, and document how users can adapt the sample for their own Pig jobs.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "U3 - Windows build support",
      "activity_description": "Run the full Gradle build on a Windows machine, catalog failures, fix path separator, line-ending, and shell-dependent build and unit-test issues, and verify a clean, repeatable Windows build.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "U4 - Windows acceptance test environment on EC2 with CI",
      "activity_description": "Provision a Windows AMI on EC2 with JDK, Gradle, and XD installed; adapt the acceptance test suite for Windows (paths, commands, services); debug and fix environment-specific failures; and create and stabilize a Jenkins CI job that runs the suite on the Windows node.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "U5 - Spark Streaming processor modules (Java lambdas and Scala)",
      "activity_description": "Design the XD stream processor module structure for Spark Streaming, implement one processor in Java using Java 8 lambdas and one in Scala, add unit and integration tests, and provide sample streams with documentation demonstrating the capabilities.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "U6 - Reference guide copyright year update",
      "activity_description": "Update the copyright message in the documentation source from 2014 to include 2015, regenerate the PDF reference guide, and verify the rendered output.",
      "most_likely_effort": 0.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "U7 - Upgrade to Spring Integration Kafka GA",
      "activity_description": "Identify Kafka changes made in XD that must be backported to Spring Integration Kafka, contribute/port those changes upstream, switch XD to the SI Kafka GA release, adapt XD's Kafka modules to the GA API, and run Kafka integration tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "U8 - Upgrade to Spring Hadoop (SHDP) GA",
      "activity_description": "Upgrade the SHDP dependency to the GA release, resolve API or behavior changes in Hadoop-dependent XD modules (including the Pig sample), and re-run the related test suites.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "Cross-cutting integration and regression testing",
      "activity_description": "Run full regression across supported platforms (including Windows) covering streams, batch jobs, Kafka, Hadoop/Pig, and Spark Streaming modules after all upgrades; investigate and fix defects found.",
      "most_likely_effort": 5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A11",
      "activity_name": "Release documentation and packaging verification",
      "activity_description": "Finalize release notes (migration, Windows support, new samples, dependency upgrades), review generated reference documentation including the PDF, and verify distribution packaging for the increment.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 64.5
  }
}
```

